# memory-ledger needs NO credentials, API keys, or secrets to run — locally
# or deployed. lib/ (the contracts, decay, contradiction, and forgetting
# engines) is deterministic and reads no external service, and the plan's
# own §5 requires this to stay true by construction — a grep-based
# architectural test asserting zero LLM-client/network imports under
# lib/contradiction/** and lib/decay/**, not merely a promise here.
#
# The one environment variable a later, deployed milestone (M2) reads is
# set FOR you by Vercel — you never configure it yourself, and local dev
# works without it:
#
#   VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA   The SHA of the commit Vercel deployed. Read by
#                           app/api/health/route.ts (added at M2) to report
#                           which commit is live. Unset during `npm run dev`;
#                           the health check falls back to a local-dev value
#                           and still runs normally.
#
# There is nothing to fill in below. If a later milestone introduces a real
# credential, it gets documented here with what it's for when that happens —
# not invented ahead of time.
